concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-319-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "319(6) Stay of proceedings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-319-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) In considering whether a stay of the POCA proceedings is in the interests of justice, the court must have regard to the following matters:  (a) that the POCA proceedings, and any criminal proceedings of a kind referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b), should proceed as expeditiously as possible;  Schedule 1  Proceeds of crime  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016 No. 15, 2016  (b) the cost and inconvenience to the Commonwealth of retaining property to which the POCA proceeding relates and being unable to expeditiously realise its proceeds;  (c) the risk of a *proceeds of crime authority suffering any prejudice (whether general or specific) in relation to the conduct of the POCA proceedings if the proceedings were stayed;  (d) whether any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the POCA proceedings were not stayed may be addressed by the court by means other than a stay of the proceedings;  (e) any orders (other than an order for the stay of the POCA proceedings) that the court could make to address any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the proceedings were not stayed. Note: Examples of orders the court could make to address any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the POCA proceedings were not stayed include an order under section 319A (closed court) or an order prohibiting the disclosure of information." ;
    skos:definition "(6) In considering whether a stay of the POCA proceedings is in the interests of justice, the court must have regard to the following matters:  (a) that the POCA proceedings, and any criminal proceedings of a kind referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or (b), should proceed as expeditiously as possible;  Schedule 1  Proceeds of crime  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016 No. 15, 2016  (b) the cost and inconvenience to the Commonwealth of retaining property to which the POCA proceeding relates and being unable to expeditiously realise its proceeds;  (c) the risk of a *proceeds of crime authority suffering any prejudice (whether general or specific) in relation to the conduct of the POCA proceedings if the proceedings were stayed;  (d) whether any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the POCA proceedings were not stayed may be addressed by the court by means other than a stay of the proceedings;  (e) any orders (other than an order for the stay of the POCA proceedings) that the court could make to address any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the proceedings were not stayed. Note: Examples of orders the court could make to address any prejudice that a person (other than a proceeds of crime authority) would suffer if the POCA proceedings were not stayed include an order under section 319A (closed court) or an order prohibiting the disclosure of information."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4d50c376216fbddfd5ec77f9350c3b5884d62d5d0b029cac6802d05dd0368328" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-319 ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must consider certain matters when deciding whether to grant a stay of proceedings." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
