concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016-sch-1-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Application provisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsection 266A(2) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as amended by this Schedule, applies in relation to the disclosure of information after the commencement of this item, whether the information was obtained before or after that commencement. (2) Subsection 315A(2) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as inserted by this Schedule, applies in relation to an application made after the commencement of this item:  (a) whether the application relates to an interest in property acquired before or after that commencement; and  Proceeds of crime  Schedule 1  No. 15, 2016 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016  (b) whether the application relates to conduct that occurred before or after that commencement. (3) Sections 319 and 319A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as inserted by this Schedule, apply in relation to proceedings instituted or commenced before or after the commencement of this item.  Schedule 2  False accounting  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016 No. 15, 2016" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subsection 266A(2) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as amended by this Schedule, applies in relation to the disclosure of information after the commencement of this item, whether the information was obtained before or after that commencement. (2) Subsection 315A(2) of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as inserted by this Schedule, applies in relation to an application made after the commencement of this item:  (a) whether the application relates to an interest in property acquired before or after that commencement; and  Proceeds of crime  Schedule 1  No. 15, 2016 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016  (b) whether the application relates to conduct that occurred before or after that commencement. (3) Sections 319 and 319A of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, as inserted by this Schedule, apply in relation to proceedings instituted or commenced before or after the commencement of this item.  Schedule 2  False accounting  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Proceeds of Crime and Other Measures) Act 2016 No. 15, 2016"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9e3c41e32d00ec52929b8482454a4e8e092981b7b771f42d3a34be9d0617c858" ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Application of amended provisions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-proceeds-of-crime-and-other-measures-act-2016.pdf, p.10" ;
